WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.960
INTRO:
NIO is nearly bankrupt.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:09.880
In the 3rd quarter of 2021, they burned $440,597,000
to keep operations afloat.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:15.410
Amongst startups and especially EV startups,
such atrocious net income figures are quite

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:21.199
common given the massive overhead associated
with manufacturing and scaling vehicle production.

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:26.130
Fortunately, most of the high-flying EV startups
have billions if not tens of billions in the

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.259
bank, so they can maintain such losses for
dozens of quarters and several years.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.432
Given this alarming situation, NIO went ahead
and completed a share offering to raise $2

00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:41.040
billion in November.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.000
This has bought them a few more quarters,
but completing share offerings in the future

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.020
is going to be significantly more difficult
given that their stock is down 80% from their

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.230
all-time highs last year.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.540
Considering all this, MacroAxis currently
gives NIO a 96% probability of bankruptcy.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.110
So, if NIO doesn’t figure out profitability
within the next couple of quarters, they’re

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.739
probably going bankrupt.

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:08.809
Just a year ago though, NIO was likely the
favorite EV stock on the market after Tesla.

00:01:08.809 --> 00:01:12.419
So, what happened to NIO?

00:01:12.419 --> 00:01:17.890
WILLIAM LI:
Taking a look back, the story of NIO dates

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.710
back to a Chinese man named William Li.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.530
William was born on August 9, 1974, on a dairy
farm in the Anhui province.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:29.989
Growing up, William’s family was rather
poor, but they highly valued education and

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.909
wanted William to get a college education.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:35.820
So, they started saving up for college as
soon as William turned 7 years old.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.269
As a kid, William would often live with his
grandparents who lived in the nearby Wuling

00:01:40.269 --> 00:01:41.269
village.

00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:45.299
This was especially influential for William
because whenever he was with his grandparents,

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:47.669
they gave him an accounting task.

00:01:47.669 --> 00:01:51.560
William was responsible for counting money
and keeping records of all the cows that his

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.669
grandfather sold.

00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:56.620
This experience didn’t lead to some insane
revelation like William figuring out the importance

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.330
of money or William learning the mechanics
of business.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:03.960
But, it did make it clear to William that
regardless of what he did in the future, he

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.870
definitely did not want to live the rest of
his life in the village herding cattle and

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:08.870
keeping records.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:13.010
So, William started focusing on leaving the
village and seeing the outside world, and

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.029
his first major opportunity to do so was of
course college.

00:02:16.029 --> 00:02:20.719
William attended Peking University in Beijing
which is actually one of the most prestigious

00:02:20.719 --> 00:02:22.219
universities in China.

00:02:22.219 --> 00:02:26.520
Apparently, it’s the center of humanity-based
studies in China and is often called “the

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.800
Harvard of China”.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:34.100
Currently, their acceptance rate sits at a
measly 0.91%, so given that William got accepted,

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.770
he clearly knew what he was doing.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:40.589
Anyway, William majored in sociology, and
one of the first things he did after enrolling

00:02:40.589 --> 00:02:44.050
was pick up a job as a deputy monitor at the
university.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:47.920
His responsibilities included leading trips
to historic places like the Great Wall of

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.380
China and helping his cohort build teamwork
skills.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:55.829
William had no complaints with the job, but
unfortunately, he would fall ill and be hospitalized

00:02:55.829 --> 00:02:56.829
for a month.

00:02:56.829 --> 00:02:59.229
And by the time he recovered, he had lost
the job.

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:03.770
This experience made William realize how dispensible
he was, and in an effort to combat this, he

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.510
would try to add a few specialties to his
skill set.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.449
This included getting a minor in computer
science and law.

00:03:09.449 --> 00:03:15.079
Soon enough, William graduated from college,
but he was still as lost as ever before, so

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:18.829
he decided to follow what interested him.

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:23.520
BITAUTO:
One of William’s biggest passions was cars,

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.950
but William wasn’t ready to do anything
nearly as ambitious as starting up an EV company.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.760
So, he gauged the business landscape, and
the most obvious opportunity he saw was the

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.760
internet.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.199
So, in 1996, William decided to combine his
passion for cars and the opportunity that

00:03:37.199 --> 00:03:41.070
came with the internet in order to found the
precursor to Bitauto.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.949
Today, Bitauto has evolved into being one
of the largest automotive publications in

00:03:44.949 --> 00:03:50.040
China, and they do everything from marketing
consultations to providing transactional services.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.669
But back in 1996, Bitauto was basically just
a blog and William was the main reporter.

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:59.550
Given the rapid growth of the internet throughout
the late 1990s and the lack of Chinese automotive

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.169
content at the time, William was able to build
up a solid following rather quickly which

00:04:04.169 --> 00:04:08.270
allowed him to go from barely making ends
meet to being pretty well off.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:12.160
Despite the evolution of his finances though,
William had no urge to stop being a reporter

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.090
and take on a more traditional role as a CEO.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.970
He says that being a reporter gave him insight
into the automotive industry that he couldn’t

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:19.970
get anywhere else.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:24.320
It wasn’t until 2000 that William stepped
back from reporting and officially founded

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.399
Bitauto Holdings.

00:04:25.399 --> 00:04:30.010
While William was initially hesitant to make
the move, once he made the move, he was fully

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.010
committed.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:34.220
He split the business up into three segments
which included the advertising and subscription

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:38.579
business, the transaction services business,
and the digital marketing solutions business.

00:04:38.579 --> 00:04:42.490
Starting with the advertising business, this
is basically what he was already doing.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:46.850
He sold advertising spots on his news portal
to automakers, dealerships, and insurance

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.850
companies.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.620
Given that all of you guys are watching YouTube,
I’m sure yall know how this works.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.440
Moving onto their transactions business, BitAuto
partnered with a leading automobile finance

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.489
platform in China called Yixin Group Limited
to provide various financial services to their

00:04:59.489 --> 00:05:00.489
customers.

00:05:00.489 --> 00:05:04.820
And finally, in terms of the digital marketing
business, given that BitAuto had achieved

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.370
moderate success on the internet, William
started to provide digital marketing consulting

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.570
services to automakers and dealerships.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.950
You know, the classic how to set up a website,
how to drive traffic to the site, how to convert

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.770
viewers into customers, and so on and so forth.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:22.400
William did this for the next 13 years which
not only made him wealthy but gave him significant

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.370
connections within the automotive world.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:26.780
And this put him in the perfect position to
startup NIO.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:32.660
NIO
Being involved in the automotive world for

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:36.649
decades at this point, it was clear to William
that EVs were the future.

00:05:36.649 --> 00:05:39.679
He wasn’t the only one that was convinced
of this future either.

00:05:39.679 --> 00:05:43.730
Basically, all of corporate China and the
government were confident the EVs were the

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.980
future, and given the pollution problem in
China, they wanted to switch over as soon

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.140
as possible.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.649
As a result, when William proposed the idea
of founding an EV startup, dozens of high-flying

00:05:53.649 --> 00:05:56.010
tech companies lined up to provide funding.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:01.590
This included Tencent, Xiaomi, Sequoia Capital,
Lenovo, Temasek, and TPG.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.450
And with that, William founded NIO in November
of 2014, but it wasn’t originally called

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.450
NIO.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:10.899
Initially, the company didn’t really have
a name, and they were simply referred to as

00:06:10.899 --> 00:06:12.120
NextEV.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:17.269
Anyway, despite all this funding and the involvement
of big players, the general public had no

00:06:17.269 --> 00:06:19.240
clue what NextEV was.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.590
Given that NextEV’s vehicles were consumer
vehicles, this wasn’t a good thing.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:27.750
So, William’s first order of business was
to generate hype around the brand and what

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.550
better way to do that than show off a flashy
sports car.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:35.230
In November of 2016, NextEV debuted the NIO
EP9 sports car.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:41.459
This car would actually become the most expensive
EV ever built clocking in at $3.48 million.

00:06:41.459 --> 00:06:47.730
The EP9 was also the fastest EV ever built
with a max speed of 217 mph.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:51.790
Despite the impressive stats, this car was
obviously not reasonable for the average person

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:54.620
in China, but this didn’t matter.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.899
NIO had intentions of mass-producing this
car.

00:06:57.899 --> 00:07:01.750
This was simply a publicity stunt like the
Tesla roadster to generate hype, and that’s

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.450
exactly what it accomplished.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:07.410
Soon enough, people from around the world
were talking about NIO’s crazy sports car

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.769
that could break 200 mph.

00:07:09.769 --> 00:07:14.280
And this gave NIO the perfect opportunity
to launch their luxury SUV, the ES8, in late

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.280
2017.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.139
The ES8 wasn’t exactly cheap, but it also
wasn’t crazy expensive either.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:25.179
It started at $67,000 which made it comfortably
affordable to well-off families.

00:07:25.179 --> 00:07:30.709
NIO’s customers and car magazines loved
the ES8, but unfortunately, this didn’t

00:07:30.709 --> 00:07:32.130
last too long.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:37.450
You see, starting in late 2018, stories of
ES8’s catching fire started to surface.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:42.230
There were only a handful of cases, but as
you would guess, this was terrible for NIO’s

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.370
public reputation.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:47.959
NIO would end up recalling the ES8 in 2019,
and NIO’s delivery numbers would subsequently

00:07:47.959 --> 00:07:49.200
jump off a cliff.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:55.710
In late 2018, NIO was delivering over 3,000
ES8s per month, but by mid-2019, they were

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.370
delivering less than 500 ES8s per month.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.800
NIO tried to combat this decline by launching
a smaller SUV called the ES6, and this did

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.780
help quite a bit especially given the lower
starting price.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:10.350
But, NIO was still in a pretty rough position
financially and reputation-wise at the end

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.350
of 2019.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:15.730
Out of nowhere though, Tesla would reveal
the Cybertruck, and Tesla stock would go to

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.190
the moon and the rest is history.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:23.349
NIO’S THREE STRIKES:
Even though NIO stock was sent to the moon

00:08:23.349 --> 00:08:29.109
along with Tesla from a low of $1 to nearly
$70, NIO was far from safe due to three main

00:08:29.109 --> 00:08:31.790
reasons starting with their investor base.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:36.300
Most of the people who invested in NIO didn’t
invest because they were confident in their

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.730
financials or optimistic about their future.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.830
In most cases, they missed out on Tesla’s
run and they didn’t want to buy into Tesla

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.830
at several hundred dollars.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:48.010
So, they looked for the next Tesla and the
most obvious choice within the stock market

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.350
was NIO.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.900
Considering this, a significant portion of
NIO’s investors were short-term investors

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.490
who were looking to make a quick buck.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:59.130
So, you can bet that these guys left as soon
as NIO started to dip substantially which

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.680
has made it significantly harder to do share
offerings and raise money.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.349
And that brings us into NIO’s second major
problem which is that they’re not profitable

00:09:07.349 --> 00:09:09.810
nor are they close to being profitable.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.470
Most of Tesla’s run occurred right after
Tesla achieved profitability after years of

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.440
struggling with model 3 production.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:45.430
In fact, Tesla neared bankruptcy on several
occasions while trying to ramp up production.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.820
And this is exactly where NIO is at right
now.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:52.960
Last year, they delivered 91,000 vehicles,
and over the next few years, they have to

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:54.140
scale to hundreds of thousands.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:10:00.399
If we take a look back at 2017, Tesla delivered
103,000 cars, and over the next few years,

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:04.270
they scaled to hundreds of thousands which
is when they faced the vast majority of their

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.380
financial problems.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:09.710
So, there’s no doubt that the next few years
will be extremely difficult for NIO given

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.500
that they’re just now entering production
hell.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:17.190
And finally, moving on to the last major factor
weighing down NIO, we have the Chinese government.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.510
Now, the Chinese government has no problems
with NIO specifically.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:24.210
In fact, they’re major proponents of the
EV revolution.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:28.440
However, they’ve been fighting a corporate
war against Jack Ma and a delisting war against

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.680
the US for the past 18 months.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:34.530
And all this uncertainty has basically crashed
the entire Chinese stock market.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:40.830
In fact, Alibaba nearly revisited IPO levels
after dropping 76% from their all-time high.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:45.100
So, until NIO sheds all of its short-term
investors, survives production hell, and the

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:49.620
Chinese government lightens up, NIO’s future
remains uncertain.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:54.599
NIO’S SAVIOR:
Despite all this uncertainty, personally,

00:10:54.599 --> 00:10:59.760
I don’t think NIO is going anywhere for
one reason which is the Chinese government.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.969
While their actions thus far have been inadvertently
hurting NIO, I’m rather confident that they

00:11:04.969 --> 00:11:06.740
won’t let NIO go bankrupt.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:11.870
For the CCP, saving NIO is not only a matter
of reducing pollution within China but a matter

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.800
of national pride.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:17.649
China really wants to beat the rest of the
world to EVs and be the first world power

00:11:17.649 --> 00:11:18.969
that makes the transition.

00:11:18.969 --> 00:11:23.070
And sacrificing one of their biggest EV producers
definitely won’t help that.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:26.620
Also, we should note that the CCP has helped
NIO in the past.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:32.700
In late 2019 when NIO was facing the recall
crisis, the CCP gave them a $1 billion bailout.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:37.840
At the time, NIO’s entire market cap was
hovering at just $1 to $2 billion.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:42.149
So, the CCP basically gave them a loan that
was the size of their market cap.

00:11:42.149 --> 00:11:47.709
Today, NIO is worth over $30 billion even
with the recent decline, so I think the CCP

00:11:47.709 --> 00:11:51.420
would just be even more willing to loan them
a couple billion if needed.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:56.800
Personally, I wouldn’t invest in NIO because
I’d rather just invest in Tesla, but with

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:02.529
that being said, given CCP support, I don’t
think NIO is going anywhere anytime soon despite

00:12:02.529 --> 00:12:04.160
their horrendous balance sheet.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.240
But that’s just what I think.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.760
Do you guys think NIO will go bankrupt?

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.490
Comment that down below.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:13.610
Also, drop a like if you hope NIO survives
and accelerates EV adoption.

